==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
{{root|is|ine-pro|*bʰuH-}}
From {{inh|is|non|búa}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*būaną}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈpuːa/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|uːa|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|bjó|bjuggu|búið}}

# {{lb|is|intransitive}} to [[reside]], to [[live]]
#: {{ux|is|Ég '''bý''' í Þýskalandi.|I '''live''' in Germany.}}
#: {{ux|is|Þar sem ég '''bý'''.|In my '''neck of the woods'''.}}
# {{lb|is|intransitive}} to [[run]] a [[farm]] or [[home]]
#: {{ux|is|Hann er hættur að '''búa'''.|He has given up '''farming'''.}}
# {{lb|is|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[prepare]]
# {{lb|is|impersonal}} used in set phrases
#: {{ux|is|Honum '''býr''' eitthvað í brjósti.|There is something on his mind.}}

====Conjugation====
{{is-conj (búa)}}

